---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FinalCTA from '~/components/FinalCTA.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About · Vicji Massage"
  description="Vicji's story: a Brazilian therapist who traveled to Thailand to study Thai Massage at the source. Now practicing in Atibaia."
  lang="en"
  path="/en/about"
>
  <section class="py-24 sm:py-32">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="label-overline mb-4">The story</div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-5xl sm:text-6xl text-ocean mb-12 leading-tight">
        From Thailand to India, and home to teach what I learned.
      </h1>

      <div class="aspect-[3/4] sm:aspect-[16/10] rounded-2xl mb-12 relative overflow-hidden bg-ocean-dark">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/photos/portrait-meditative.webp" />
          <img
            src="/photos/portrait-meditative.jpg"
            alt="Vicji in a meditative moment during a session"
            class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </picture>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-ocean-dark/40 via-transparent to-transparent"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-soft space-y-6">
        <p class="font-display italic text-2xl text-ink leading-snug">
          Thai Massage is an ancient practice of healing, respect, compassion, and care for the other. Its benefits go far beyond the physical body, and can be felt for days after a session.
        </p>

        <p>
          My name is Vicji. I am Brazilian, and massage came into my life as a question, not a profession. I wanted to understand how the body holds what we live through, and how it lets go when it receives the right care.
        </p>

        <p>
          That question took me to Thailand, where I trained as a massage therapist at the source of the tradition. I learned traditional Thai practice: pressure along the energy lines (sen), passive stretches, meditative pace, working with the breath, and the spiritual dimension that holds it all together. I learned that massage was born integrated, not fragmented.
        </p>

        <p>
          From there I went to India, where I immersed myself in yoga. I deepened my understanding of the body as an energetic system: the chakras, the flows, the blockages, and what makes a practice actually heal. Between these two formations, I lived many experiences around the world that shaped how I see the body, energy, and presence.
        </p>

        <p>
          I came back to Brazil because I felt this work was missing here. We live at a pace that hurts the body in layers, and most massages on the market only treat the physical symptom, not the root. Today, I am the only practitioner in Brazil offering this integrated approach: traditional Thai Massage technique combined with the energetic understanding I carry with me.
        </p>

        <p>
          I see clients in Atibaia, at Espaço Clô. Later this year I move to Itacaré, bringing the practice close to the sea.
        </p>

        <p>
          Every session I give is an extension of what I learned: presence, respect for the body in front of me, and time. No rush. No empty technique. Just the work.
        </p>

        <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-ink-muted">
          Khòp khun kráp 🙏<br />
          With love and presence,<br />
          Vicji
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="divider-ornament"></div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-sand-deep/30">
          <div class="label-overline mb-2">Thailand</div>
          <p class="text-ink">
            Massage therapist training
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm mt-2">
            Traditional Thai Massage, learned at the source of the tradition.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-sand-deep/30">
          <div class="label-overline mb-2">India</div>
          <p class="text-ink">
            Yoga formation
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm mt-2">
            Understanding the body as an energetic system. Chakras, flows, spiritual practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-sand-deep/30">
          <div class="label-overline mb-2">World</div>
          <p class="text-ink">
            The only one in Brazil
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm mt-2">
            Offering this integrated approach of traditional massage combined with energetic practice.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCTA lang="en" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/en/' },
    { name: 'About', href: '/en/about' },
  ]} />
</BaseLayout>
